  "id": "thepennydrops",
  "neon": "#ffd060",
  "note": "THE PENNY DROPS — the amusement arcade at the foot of Meltwater Row.\n\nThe tile's prose: a deep narrow shed with no front wall. The whole street elevation is a roller\nshutter, up from noon until whenever she decides, so the building opens straight onto the pavement\nand the light comes out at ankle height and lies across the road in a bright rectangle you can see\nfrom the top of Meltwater Row. Above the opening, in bulbs, about a third of them out: THE PENNY\nDROPS.\n\nSo the front is one opening the width of the shed with the roller drum over it, lit hard from\ninside, and a pool of that light on the road. The name is in bulbs on a board over the drum. The\nshed behind is plain brick with a shallow barrel roof.",
